[Prepped for the final run with a Valk]
>I'm pretty paranoid about unleashing the Wizard.  I've carved a two
>square wide tunnel through hell (connecting the upstairs and
>downstairs of each level -- someone talked about doing this a long
>time ago, and the advice stuck), and I'm thinking about turning around
>and doing it through the main dungeon.  Would this be wise?  Or am I
>just being crazy?

I've never bothered, except to trim some really enormous diversions out of
the main dungeon. However, now is a good time to leave a stash of the
things you will want on the Planes on DL 1 (and, if you have a vast
surplus of holy water, etc., to leave another stash at the Castle), and
you could dig round some of the larger diversions if you see fit.

The most important thing to remember is that once the Wizard is dead for
the first time, your job is not to fight everything, but to keep moving.
Only fight if you cannot maneuver, or to keep something scary off your
back by killing it.

>I have Mjollnir and GoP, I've been wearing a ring of searching and a
>+3 ring of damage control and an Amulet of ESP (reflection from
>Perseus' shield) People talk about rings of free action like they are
>an essential part of every ascension,

I don't think people do, not least because the primary advocates of them
mostly ascended a few times before they were added to the game.

Basically, free action protects against a death which is unlikely, but if
it came up would be utterly out of your hands. It's by no means vital, but
I'd rather have it than +3 increase damage - however, if I didn't have it
I would not hesitate to attempt the final run anyway.

I'd also suggest you may want a weapon that works on shock-resistant
beasties - and as a backup in case you throw Mojo and lose it; and on a
first ascension an AoLS has a lot to recommend it, at least in reserve -
not that the monster-tracking from the AoESP is not very handy.

